# The JavaScript profile's support table

> **DRAFTED, NOT ISSUED.** Release gate 11 issues no support table until a named human has recorded
> a decision on every relevant code unit, and none has: `HUMAN_REVIEW.md` is unsigned and every unit
> reads `PENDING`. This document is the table JS-10 will issue, kept true of the checkout by rules
> **N34**, **N35** and **N36** so that issuing it is a signature and not a rewrite. Until then nothing
> here is a support claim: a row says what the checkout does and what evidence shows it, and no row
> says more.

Drafted 2026-10-05 under proposed [JSD-0060](decisions/0060-the-support-table-drafted.md), phase F9's
slice R2. Roadmap [section 22](roadmap.gates.md#22-release-gates)'s release gate 1 and
[section 19](roadmap.delivery.md#js-10--baselines-packaging-the-support-table-and-the-release-gate)'s
JS-10 name what it must carry.

**Its vocabulary never reads as a bare yes.** A row is one of: **Implemented** (the checkout does it,
and the evidence cell names what shows it), **Implemented, partly** (with what is missing named),
**Not provided** (with the deterministic failure a program or a host meets), **Excluded** (by a named
decision), **Held** (an amendment this profile would ask of the core, with what stands meanwhile), or
**Not declared** (a descriptor row this profile leaves undeclared). Every row has an evidence cell
naming a rule or a retained artifact.

---

