before review. What each has been shown to do:

| RID | What has been shown | Status | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| `linux-x64` | Every composition root published and run under JIT, trimmed self-contained and Native AOT, every exit zero; the measurement lane's two arms | **Not claimed**: published and run, not reviewed | [`evidence/js-7-001/README.md`](evidence/js-7-001/README.md); [`evidence/js-10-001/README.md`](evidence/js-10-001/README.md) |
| `win-x64` | Published and run under JIT, trimmed self-contained and Native AOT | **Not claimed**: published and run, not reviewed | [`evidence/js-1/README.md`](evidence/js-1/README.md) |
| `android-x64` | Run on an emulator under Mono, without trimming or AOT | **Not claimed**: an emulator is not a device | [`evidence/js-android-001/README.md`](evidence/js-android-001/README.md) |
| `android-arm64` | Published, not run | **Not claimed**: no device | [`evidence/js-android-001/README.md`](evidence/js-android-001/README.md) |
| `linux-arm64`, `win-arm64`, `osx-arm64`, `osx-x64` | Nothing retained; the core's CI lane publishes on some | **Not claimed**: no retained collection | [`../../../docs/support.md`](../../../docs/support.md) section 3 |

